{
 "_comment": "LTX-2.3 IMAGE-to-video with generated audio. Best of both worlds for character work: the keyframe locks the character design (which pure text-to-video cannot do across shots), and LTX is still ~8x faster than Wan. Node 23 LTXVImgToVideoInplace writes the start image into the video latent; strength 1.0 = hold the keyframe exactly, lower it (0.6-0.8) to let the model reinterpret.",
 "_notes": [
  "length must be 8n+1 (97 = 4.04s @24fps, 145 = 6.04s).",
  "ManualSigmas on node 30 is the 8-step distilled schedule - do not swap in a normal scheduler.",
  "CFG stays at 1.0; the model is CFG-distilled.",
  "LTXVPreprocess img_compression 18 matches the official i2v template; it conditions the model to expect clean input."
 ],
